cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use arabic-bib, please cite it as below."
title: "arabic-bib: Arabic bibliographic text (normalisation, author names, death years, Hijri dates, editions, file names)"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free Python library and command line for Arabic bibliographic text: search and display
  normalisation that keeps the original, classical author-name parsing (ism, nasab, kunya, laqab, nisba, shuhra)
  and matching, death-year and century parsing, tabular Hijri-Gregorian conversion, edition statements,
  book-name composition under configurable profiles, and file-name audit.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Benjelloun
    given-names: Khalid
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kmbenjel/arabic-bib"
url: "https://warraq.benjelloun.dev/arabic-bib/"
keywords:
  - Arabic
  - bibliography
  - library catalogues
  - author names
  - Hijri calendar
  - text normalisation
